course: dictionary
lesson: 31
title: Abuse: cruel treatment, rude words and misuse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Abuse is a word with a few meanings. As a noun it can mean using something wrongly or too much, cruel or violent treatment of a person or animal, or rude, insulting words. As a verb, to abuse someone means to treat them cruelly, and to abuse something means to use it badly or unfairly.
explain: Use the context to find which meaning fits. «Many grassroots referees are teenagers, and abuse from the touchline is a big reason referees quit.» Shouting from the side of the pitch is the clue, so abuse means rude, insulting shouts here.
explain: «Trolling means sending many cruel messages online; you can disagree strongly with someone without abusing them.» The sentence says you can disagree with someone without being cruel to them. So abusing them means treating them cruelly and hurtfully.
fact: «Abuse» can mean rude, insulting words, as in «verbal abuse».
fact: «Abuse» can also mean cruel or violent treatment of a person or animal.
fact: «Abuse of power» means using power unfairly.
fact: If anyone hurts you or treats you cruelly, it is never your fault. Tell a trusted adult or call a helpline.
exercise: «Many grassroots referees are teenagers, and abuse from the touchline is a big reason referees quit.» What does abuse mean here? | A kind pat on the back | *Rude, insulting shouts | A new pair of boots | A fast run down the pitch
exercise: «Trolling means sending many cruel messages online; you can disagree strongly with someone without abusing them.» What does abusing them mean? | Giving them a present | *Treating them cruelly or hurtfully | Agreeing with them | Asking them a question
exercise: If someone hurts you or treats you cruelly, what should you do? | Hit back harder | Keep it secret and hope it stops | Post about it online for everyone to see | *Tell a trusted adult or call a helpline
test: Which phrase means using power unfairly? | Full power | *Abuse of power | Power cut | Power nap
test: «After England lost the Euro 2020 final on penalties, three players who missed were racially abused online.» What is the best thing to do with a hateful post? | *Report it, and tell a trusted adult | Share it to show your friends | Reply with worse insults
exam: Which word means the same as abuse in «verbal abuse»? | *Insults | Silence | Kindness | Speed
